letter e What is meant by "restriction of movement" is restricting the movement of a wife or child in developing their potential both for economic and social purposes such as prohibiting them from gathering and socializing in the community and restricting the movement of relatives such as preventing domestic workers or drivers from communicating or having contact with their families.

